# KOVA — Always-Apply Cursor Rule
# Stack: Vue 3 (Composition API) · TypeScript · Vite 7 · Tailwind CSS 4
#        Supabase · Vercel AI SDK · Bun
# Built on: open-pencil/open-pencil (MIT fork)

You are adding Kova's SaaS layer ON TOP of OpenPencil's working engine.
Never rebuild what already works. Before writing any code, read the relevant
existing file in the repo. Do not reconstruct behavior from memory or docs.

---

## HARD CONSTRAINTS

### Never modify:
- `packages/core/` — tools, figma-api.ts, schema.ts, renderer, scene graph,
  Yoga layout, Kiwi codec. All read-only reference.
- ToolLoopAgent and DirectChatTransport from Vercel AI SDK.
- The Yjs / y-indexeddb local persistence layer.
- The editor UI: canvas, toolbar, layers panel, properties panel, AI chat layout.

### Never do:
- Rebuild canvas, renderer, or scene graph.
- Build a custom Anthropic adapter (use @ai-sdk/anthropic).
- Build a custom agentic loop (use ToolLoopAgent).
- Build /api/generate for AI logic (pipeline runs in browser via DirectChatTransport).
- Build a "compiler" for tool calls (tools execute directly against FigmaAPI).
- Output HTML emails (Kova exports images).
- Use React, Next.js, or PixiJS.
- Use Zod in the tool layer — valibot only (src/ai/tools.ts and dependencies).
- Expose ANTHROPIC_API_KEY to the browser.
- Reference old Kova code (React/PixiJS/Next.js). It is dead.

### use-chat.ts — extreme care:
- The SYSTEM_PROMPT constant stays word-for-word unchanged.
- buildSystemPrompt() APPENDS Kova content after SYSTEM_PROMPT. Never replaces.
- Before modifying this file, read the actual file in the repo first.

