## CODING STANDARDS

**Vue 3:** Always `<script setup lang="ts">`. Composition API only.
ref() for primitives, reactive() for objects, computed() for derived state.
Typed defineProps<{}>() and defineEmits<{}>().

**TypeScript:** No `any`. No implicit `any`. Prefer `interface` over `type` for
object shapes. Avoid enums — use `as const` maps. Strict null checks.

**Naming:** Directories lowercase-dashed. Components PascalCase.vue.
Composables useCamelCase.ts. Booleans: isX, hasX, canX. Handlers: handleX.

**Pinia:** Composition API setup stores only. One store per domain.
Don't put OpenPencil editor state in Pinia.

**Tailwind CSS 4:** Utility classes for all new UI. No custom CSS for new pages.
No @apply unless genuinely necessary. No inline styles.

**Quality:** Max ~40 lines per function. No magic strings/numbers. No console.log
in committed code. Every async UI op needs isLoading + error state.
